{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low-bias: model forecasts are systematically below realized prices, especially during rising regimes. Apply an upward level shift (larger for longer horizons).",
    "Trend/lag error: model underreacts to upside momentum—after a turn higher, it takes ~5–15 days to catch up. Add a momentum term: if last 5–10 days are up, lift the whole path, with increasing lift beyond day ~10.",
    "Horizon-dependent underestimation: errors widen with forecast horizon (days ~15–30 most affected). Use a ramping correction (small +0–1 EUR early, larger +2–5 EUR late, conditional on positive trend).",
    "Upside tail miss: model fails to capture late-horizon rallies/spikes (e.g., outcomes push to high-60s while forecasts stay mid-60s). Add a convexity kicker: when spot is above its 20–30d MA and MA slope > 0, increase upper quantiles/late-horizon levels.",
    "Too much mean-reversion after dips: following local lows, model expects reversion down/flat, but realized path rebounds more strongly. Reduce mean-reversion strength when price is below MA but MA slope is turning up."
  ]
}
